    <h2>FAQ</h2>

    <h3>Is Runway Gen-3 better than Pika 2.0?</h3>
    <p>Runway Gen-3 is better for professional video production with higher resolution, more consistent motion, and a full editing suite. Pika 2.0 is better for creative, stylized video generation and rapid experimentation. For commercial and professional work, Runway wins. For creative exploration and social content, Pika wins.</p>

    <h3>Which is more affordable, Runway or Pika?</h3>
    <p>Pika is more affordable. Pika Pro starts at $10 per month, while Runway Standard starts at $15 per month. Both offer free tiers with watermarked exports. For budget-conscious creators, Pika delivers more value per dollar. For professional users who need higher resolution and editing tools, Runway is worth the premium.</p>

    <h3>Can I use Runway Gen-3 and Pika 2.0 together?</h3>
    <p>Yes. Many creators use both tools in their workflow. Runway excels at producing high-quality base footage with consistent motion, while Pika is ideal for creative stylization and generating multiple variations quickly. The combined cost starts at $25 per month and covers both professional and creative use cases.</p>

    <h3>Does Runway Gen-3 offer a free tier?</h3>
    <p>Yes. Runway offers a free tier with 125 credits and watermarked exports. This is enough to evaluate the platform and produce a few test clips. Paid plans remove the watermark and add higher resolution exports plus access to the full editing suite.</p>

    <h3>Which AI video generator is better for beginners?</h3>
    <p>Pika 2.0 is better for beginners. Its interface is simpler and more intuitive, and users can produce stylized clips within minutes without tutorials. Runway Gen-3 has a steeper learning curve because of its professional editing tools and more complex generation parameters. For first-time users, Pika is the easier starting point.</p>

    <h3>Can I use Runway and Pika videos for commercial projects?</h3>
    <p>Yes. Both platforms grant commercial usage rights on their paid plans. Runway's paid tiers include commercial licensing suitable for client work and advertising. Pika's paid plans also permit commercial use. Always review the current terms for the plan you purchase before distributing content commercially.</p>

